  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **Fork sync.** The fork `NeoTech/solidcore` `main` was 0 commits ahead and 300 commits behind `tangency-labs/solidcore` `main`. It took the 300 upstream commits by a fast-forward (GitHub merge-upstream). There was no force-push. The fork is now equal to upstream at `fa67b3f560b7a8d59e99cb728f72f85e91dee2da` (2026-11-23). The old pin was `2016386442dfee3b2a0c3a1bfdd4017c5254dac8` (2026-11-19).\n- **Pin.** `crates/kernel/Cargo.toml` pins the six solidcore crates at the full new rev.\n- **Cargo.lock.** Only the six solidcore packages change (`solidcore`, `-step`, `-convert`, `-ops`, `-record`, `-tess`).\n- **#3742.** The unused workspace line `truck-polymesh = \"=0.6.0\"` is removed. The build does not print the warning now. `truck-polymesh` stays in `Cargo.lock` as a dependency of `truck-meshalgo`.\n- **LICENSES.md.** The solidcore section names the new rev. The NOTICE and LICENSE blobs at `fa67b3f5` are the same as at `55d0e763`.\n- **One code change** in `camcraft_geometry::step_diag::record_parses` (see \"Readings\").\n\n## Dependencies and licences\n\n| Package | Change | Licence |\n|---|---|---|\n| solidcore, solidcore-step, solidcore-convert, solidcore-ops, solidcore-record, solidcore-tess | rev `2016386` -> `fa67b3f5` | Apache-2.0 (workspace licence, unchanged) |\n| serde 1.0.229 | `solidcore-ops` uses it as a dependency now (it was a dev-dependency). The package was already in the lock. | MIT OR Apache-2.0 |\n\nNo new package is in `Cargo.lock`. Thus `needs-maintainer` is not set.\n\n## Readings: the pins that moved, and why\n\nEach file is still refused or still measured exactly. No assert was widened.\n\n1. `twisted_flank_off.step` (kernel `step_agreement` row, kernel, geometry and app `step_twisted_flank`). Still refused as `#117`. The reader now builds the pcurves, and the vertex check refuses the solid: `#117 at check: a vertex sits 3.430e-1 mm off its edges (limit 1e-3)`. It was `#117 at read: pcurves failed on ...`. The new message does not name face #93, so the app pin drops that one assert.\n2. `edge_gap_021_stated_5mm.step` (kernel and geometry `step_edge_gap`). It was kept by the reader and refused by the machining mesh at the chord. Now the kernel gap check refuses it at the read, and names the 0.02 mm cap and the stated 5 mm. This is an earlier refusal of the same file.\n3. `cube-chamfer-all-12-d2` (kernel `blend`). The volume moves from 802.667 to 808.000 mm3. Upstream \"retire the fillet_chamfer_corner flag (chamfer-corner event is the only chamfer corner) (#21269)\" makes three equal chamfers meet in one mitred vertex, with no flat bevel triangle. The closed form drops the d^3/12 tetrahedron for each corner. It agrees with the new solid exactly (|dV| < 1e-9).\n4. `provoke_face_left_out_edge_not_sampled_and_lenient` case 3 (kernel `machining_mesh_shortfalls`). The self-crossing inner loop now gives `NotWatertight { open: 6 }`, not `Lenient`. It is still a refusal. No test reaches the `Lenient` arm now: follow-up #3800.\n5. `step_nesting::a_record_at_the_cap_still_imports` and `parentheses_inside_text_are_not_counted` (app). The new Part 21 parser holds the counts of a text to the density of its own length (one parameter for each 4 bytes). `step_diag` probes each DATA record alone in a short frame. Thus a dense legal record was refused as a syntax error, and the import failed. The probe now reads `TooManyParams`, `TooManyRecords` and `TooManyEntities` as \"no syntax fault\". The parse of the whole file still applies the limits. New pin: `step_diag::a_dense_legal_record_is_not_named` (red without the fix, green with it).\n\nNo toolpath pin moved.\n\n## Tests run (CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6, -j 6, no CARGO_TARGET_DIR)\n\n- `camcraft-kernel`: the full debug suite, green (`step_agreement` 29/29, `step_edge_gap`, `step_twisted_flank`, `blend`, `machining_mesh*`, `step_import`, `import_corpus`, `corrupt_input`, `solidcraft_*`, `agreement`, lib).\n- `camcraft-geometry`: the full debug suite, green, with `step_diag::a_dense_legal_record_is_not_named`.\n- `camcraft-app`, targeted: `import`, `import_step_*` (13 binaries), `step_nesting`, `adaptive_fig8_crossing`, `lead_approach`, `adaptive_pass_start`, `flute_reach`, `feature_edge_g1_join`, `shoulder_adaptive`. All green.\n- Targeted heavy step (release, `--ignored`): `adaptive_fig8_crossing::adaptive2d_on_fig8_model_in_tight_stock_has_no_crossings_and_posts` and `adaptive2d_on_fig8_stock_excluding_top_face_has_no_crossings_and_posts`: pass.\n- #2849 known-fail `shoulder_adaptive::fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works` (release): still fails at the `// known-fail-assert` line with `EM-0800-4FL ends at selected face (dist 31.406, r 4)`. The new solidcore does not fix it. The marker stays valid.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -D warnings` and clippy on `camcraft-app --test import_step_twisted_flank`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full quick plan (1193 steps: the lock change reaches each crate). The UI suites and the other app binaries did not run.\n- The full heavy lanes and the light lane. They run at the cut.\n- Linux and macOS builds. The change adds no platform code.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3767-solidcore-bump.md`.\n\nChangelog: STEP import uses solidcore at the newest upstream commit (fa67b3f5). A dense but legal STEP record is no longer refused as a syntax error. The kernel builds three equal chamfers at one corner as one mitred vertex.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3742\nFixes #3767\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
